2. CJK glyph outlines (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
-------------------------------------------------

The Chinese glyph outlines in fonts/ are derived from Noto Serif CJK SC
Medium (Source Han Serif), copyright (c) 2017-2022 Adobe
(http://www.adobe.com/) and other contributors, licensed under the SIL
Open Font License, Version 1.1.

The complete license text is in OFL.txt. In summary, the OFL requires:

  - the copyright notice and the license text accompany any copy;
  - modified versions are distributed only under the OFL;
  - the font software is not sold by itself;
  - Reserved Font Names, where declared, are not used by derivatives;
  - the original authors' names are not used to promote a modified version.

The conversion from CFF cubic outlines to TrueType quadratic outlines,
the scaling to 2000 units per em, the metric unification and the composite
assembly were added for this project (c) 2026 Moirania, as recorded in
FONTLOG.txt.

The Reserved Font Name "Noto" is not used as the family name of this
composite font.


3. Upstream Latin outlines (proprietary, NOT open source)
----------------------------------------------------------

Anthropic Serif Web Text and related names are proprietary brand assets of
Anthropic, PBC. No public font license from the rights holder is known to
accompany the upstream Latin font, and it is NOT covered by the MIT license
above, NOT covered by the SIL Open Font License, and NOT relicensed by this
repository.

The files under fonts/ retain the complete Latin outline set of that
upstream font together with its original internal family name. Publishing,
redistributing or using those files in a product may require permission
from the rights holder. The maintainer of this repository chose to publish
the full files in a public repository and assumes responsibility for that
decision. This repository grants no rights to the upstream font and makes
no representation that such rights have been obtained.

See docs/COMPLIANCE.md for the full analysis and for a conservative
publication path that does not redistribute the upstream outlines.


